For Xerox the market-cap arithmetic is $\begin{aligned}
\text{Xerox market cap}
&\approx (1.4\ \text{billion shares})(\$11.80) \\
&\approx \$16.4\text{--}16.5\ \text{billion}.\end{aligned}$ So the market valued Xerox above its book shareholder equity of about $11.9 billion.

